<section class="sec fi">
  <div class="wrap tc">
    <div class="tag">Your questions answered</div>
    <h2 class="h2">Still thinking about it? <span class="grad-text">We've heard it all.</span></h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">Will creatine make me look bulky or masculine?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">This is the #1 creatine myth and it's completely false. Creatine doesn't affect your hormone levels, doesn't increase testosterone, and doesn't cause masculine physical characteristics. What it does is help you build lean, functional muscle — the kind that makes you look toned and athletic, not masculinized. Many women report improved body composition (more defined, less soft) with creatine use. The "bulky" fear comes from misunderstanding what creatine actually does at a cellular level.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">What exactly is creatine monohydrate and how does it work?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Creatine monohydrate is a naturally occurring compound your body makes from amino acids and stores in your muscles. It plays a critical role in ATP production — the energy molecule that powers every muscular contraction. When you supplement with creatine, you're increasing your muscles' energy reserve, allowing them to perform more work before fatiguing and recover faster afterward. It's not a stimulant, it's not a hormone, and it doesn't depend on caffeine or any artificial mechanism to work.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">How long does it take to feel results?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Most people notice improved workout endurance within 1–2 weeks of consistent daily use. Strength gains typically become noticeable around weeks 2–4. Recovery improvements often show up within the first 10 days. The key word is consistent — creatine works by gradually saturating your muscle cells, which requires daily intake. That's exactly why we made X11 taste like something you want to take every morning.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">Do I need to "load" creatine or take it at a specific time?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Loading (taking 20g/day for 5–7 days) was a strategy to speed up saturation, but current research shows it's unnecessary — you reach the same saturation after 3–4 weeks at 5g/day. Timing also doesn't matter much. Morning, pre-workout, post-workout, with a meal — all produce equivalent results. Just take it daily. Consistency is the only variable that actually matters.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">Are these actually 100% vegan? What about the gummy texture?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Yes — completely, unambiguously vegan. The secret is pectin, a plant-derived ingredient from fruit peel that creates the same satisfying chewy texture as gelatin but contains zero animal products. Most gummies on the market — supplement gummies, vitamin gummies, candy gummies — use gelatin derived from animal collagen. We developed our formula specifically using pectin so vegans don't have to choose between ethics and effectiveness.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">Can I take these if I don't work out?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Yes. While creatine is most famous for athletic performance, it also has documented cognitive benefits regardless of activity level — improved working memory, reduced mental fatigue, and mood support. Research suggests creatine may be particularly beneficial for vegetarians and vegans, and for women during periods of high stress. That said, combining creatine with resistance training will dramatically amplify your results.</div></div></div>
      <div class="fi2"><button class="fq" aria-expanded="false">What does it taste like — honestly?<div class="fplus">+</div></button><div class="fa"><div class="fa-in">Like a high-quality strawberry gummy candy. Bright, sweet, slightly tart — like a premium strawberry bear, not a vitamin with strawberry perfume. We worked with flavor specialists for months to avoid the chemical aftertaste that plagues most supplement gummies. Our most common review phrase is "I was expecting it to be bad but it's actually really good."</div></div></div>
